//? Title: Golden-section search: reuse a probe, check the bracket
//? Subtitle: Actual native brackets, callback work and the limits of finite comparisons
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A scalar objective can be expensive to evaluate even when its derivative is unavailable. Given a finite interval, we want a location with a large objective value while controlling the number of evaluations. Golden-section search reuses one interior probe whenever it discards part of the interval. This report derives the fixed-ratio contraction, follows actual native search states, and distinguishes a small bracket from an accurate maximizer. Rounded objective values, flat tails and adjacent floating-point endpoints provide explicit counterexamples to unconditional accuracy claims. Native traces expose complete execution events and callback counts with an online record limit.
)

\toc

> See one actual reuse before the formula

On [0,4], the objective −(x−3)² has its unique maximum at 3. Two initial
probes give different values, so the search can discard the left part. The
surviving right probe becomes the new left probe, carrying its cached value.
The new right probe costs one fresh evaluation. The final midpoint is evaluated
once more, even in this deliberately one-update run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/golden_reuse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/golden_section_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const auto t=dm::algorithms::golden_section_trace([](double x){return -(x-3)*(x-3);},0,4,0,1,3);
 const auto& e=t.events[1];
 std::print("| state | a | b | c | d | f(c) | f(d) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(int j=0;j<2;++j){const auto& q=j?e.after:e.before;std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",j?"After":"Before",q.a,q.b,q.c,q.d,q.fc,q.fd);}
 std::print("\nKept right {}; reused old d as new c {}; cached value unchanged {}; actual callbacks {}; complete records {}; stop {}. Final midpoint {:.9f}, value {:.9f}.\n",e.kept_right,e.after.c==e.before.d,e.after.fc==e.before.fd,t.run.evaluations,t.events.size(),dm::algorithms::golden_stop_name(t.run.stop),t.run.result.argmax,t.run.result.value);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1050);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=5.1;box.height=2.1;box.font_size=21;
 d.node("old",{0,0},std::format("Before: [{:.3f}, {:.3f}]\nc = {:.3f}, f(c) = {:.3f}\nd = {:.3f}, f(d) = {:.3f}",e.before.a,e.before.b,e.before.c,e.before.fc,e.before.d,e.before.fd),box)
  .node("new",{8,0},std::format("After: [{:.3f}, {:.3f}]\nreused c = {:.3f}\nnew d = {:.3f}",e.after.a,e.after.b,e.after.c,e.after.d),box)
  .edge("old","new","f(c) < f(d)")
  .text({4,2.3},"Keep [c,b]; reuse old d and its value",24)
  .text({4,-2.3},std::format("2 initial + 1 new probe + 1 final midpoint = {} calls",t.run.evaluations),22)
  .save_svg("build/golden_reuse.svg");
 if(!e.kept_right||e.after.c!=e.before.d||t.run.evaluations!=4)throw std::runtime_error("actual reuse");

}
