\caption(The table samples actual records at multiples of five and at the final update. Both curves use positive widths without a floor. The final midpoint evaluation increases the total callback count from 53 to 54.)
\alttext(A log10 width plot compares the actual native bracket widths with three times rho to the update count. The printed result retains the failed containment check and distinguishes absolute location error from final half-width.)

The rounded original display, “1.559”, hides this distinction. Neither the old
result layout nor the new diagnostics claim an accuracy certificate. The final
value is a fresh midpoint evaluation, not the largest cached sample. Callback
exceptions propagate, and the callable is passed by value; captured references
can still change external state.

> Count callbacks, including initialization and the final midpoint

Two initial evaluations plus t fresh probes plus one midpoint give t+3 actual
calls. The alternative below is a hypothetical count for recomputing both
probes at every step; that search is not executed. These counts measure neither
machine instructions nor elapsed time. An update limit of zero still makes
three calls; it does not skip evaluating the objective.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/golden_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/golden_section_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 std::vector<double> update,actual,recompute;
 std::print("| requested update cap | completed updates | predicted calls | actual calls | hypothetical two-new-probe calls |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(int cap:{0,1,2,4,8,16,32}){
  std::size_t counted=0;auto r=dm::algorithms::golden_section_run([&](double x){++counted;return -(x-.3)*(x-.3);},0,1,0,cap);
  const auto predicted=std::size_t(r.result.iterations)+3,hypothetical=2*std::size_t(r.result.iterations)+3;
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",cap,r.result.iterations,predicted,r.evaluations,hypothetical);
  update.push_back(r.result.iterations);actual.push_back(r.evaluations);recompute.push_back(hypothetical);
  if(r.evaluations!=counted||counted!=predicted)throw std::runtime_error("callback count");
 }
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.line(update,recompute,"hypothetical",{217,119,6},2).line(update,actual,"actual",{37,99,235},2).points(update,actual,"actual",{37,99,235},4)
  .legend({"Hypothetical: 3 + 2t","Actual native calls: 3 + t"},{{217,119,6},{37,99,235}}).title("Reuse saves one callback per completed update")
  .xlab("Completed updates t").ylab("Objective calls").x_limits(0,32).y_limits(0,90).save_svg("build/golden_work.svg");

}
